The model connectivity, original neuron IDs, and paper neuron selections in
connectome.js and metadata.json are a lossless repacking of the data distributed
by Philip Shiu and Nico Spiller in their Drosophila_brain_model repository and
official research archive, https://doi.org/10.17617/3.CZODIW. The archive explicitly
licenses the v630 connectivity and completeness files under the MIT License.
Their original MIT notice follows below.

FlyWire's general public-data guidelines specify Creative Commons Attribution-
NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0):
https://flywire.ai/guidelines
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/

This package retains both source notices and treats underlying connectome reuse
as noncommercial. The MIT archive notice is not interpreted as overriding the
upstream FlyWire terms. This is not a claim of a choice of alternative licenses.
The dataset may be copied and adapted for noncommercial purposes with source
attribution, a link to the applicable terms, and an indication of modifications.
No additional rights over the biological source data are claimed here.

Underlying biological reconstruction: FlyWire Consortium, Dorkenwald et al.,
Neuronal wiring diagram of an adult brain, Nature (2024),
https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-024-07558-y.
Neuron annotations: Schlegel et al., Whole-brain annotation and multi-connectome
cell typing of Drosophila, Nature (2024),
https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-024-07686-5.
Neurotransmitter predictions: Eckstein, Bates et al., Cell (2024),
https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2024.03.016.
Computational model and selected sensory/motor identities: Shiu et al.,
A Drosophila computational brain model reveals sensorimotor processing,
Nature (2024), https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-024-07763-9.

This independent adaptation has no affiliation with or endorsement by these
authors or institutions. All source neuron and connection identities are
preserved. Storage format changes are documented in metadata.json.

